 "capsule": "The Federated Republic of Brazil denotes the state as reconstituted by the January 1967 Constitution, which formally renamed the country the Federative Republic of Brazil while the military regime installed after the 1964 coup ruled through successive general-presidents—Costa e Silva, Médici, Geisel and Figueiredo—exercising dictatorial powers under Institutional Acts, especially the notorious AI-5 of 1968. Gradual liberalization ('abertura') from the mid-1970s culminated in the 1985 return of civilian government under José Sarney, though the military-era federal structure persisted until the 1988 constitution. This authoritarian-to-transitional federal era is distinct from the preceding centralized 'Unitary State' and the post-1988 democratic 'Republic of Brazil' sharing this identifier.",
